{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"plan","namespace":"","artifact_type":"","name":"P9e17b896"},"owner_reference":"#3276","content":"{\"plan_id\":\"P9e17b896\",\"feature\":\"contract-verification-async-reporting\",\"version\":\"1.0.0\",\"description\":\"\",\"goal\":\"Make bare Agent()-dispatched dh agents deliver their findings through a durable backend destination instead of a synchronous return value, at both defect sites (contract-verification/implement-feature step 4a, and groom/error.md's Agent Failure procedure), and stop dispatch-contract/SKILL.md from authorizing the anti-pattern that regenerates it.\",\"context\":\"# Plan Context \\u2014 #3276 Contract-Verification Async Reporting\\n\\n## The defect in one paragraph\\n\\nUnder this runtime's dispatch semantics, a bare non-team `Agent()` call returns only a\\n\\\"Spawned successfully\\\" acknowledgment \\u2014 the subagent's plain-text output is never visible to\\nthe dispatcher. Three files encode the opposite assumption. `agents/contract-verification.md:151`\\nsays \\\"Your finding is your response. The dispatcher reads it there \\u2014 you register no artifact and\\nwrite no task state.\\\" `skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` lines 187-198 branch on that\\nnever-arriving value. `skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/error.md` step 3\\ndispatches `dh:task-worker` asking it to \\\"Report: last_success, first_failure, failure_type\\\" and\\nfeeds those into a Mermaid decision tree at lines 30-40 that can therefore never reach its\\nEscalation branch. `skills/dispatch-contract/SKILL.md:11` is the doctrine authorizing the pattern.\\n\\nThere is no error, no timeout, no blocked state. \\\"No violations found\\\" is byte-for-byte\\nindistinguishable from \\\"the finding was dropped.\\\" That silence is why this is P2.\\n\\n## The fix pattern (same pattern, deliberately different destinations)\\n\\nEach agent writes its own result to a backend destination named in its own agent file; the\\nconsumer reads it back. Per `skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md`'s `<result_destination>` primary\\nrule \\u2014 \\\"Put your result where your own agent file says\\\" \\u2014 this resolves routing before the\\nartifact fallback is ever reached.\\n\\nThe two sites use different destinations because their consumption shapes differ:\\n\\n- **contract-verification \\u2192 `backlog_groom` on the Concerns section.** Accumulating, human-facing,\\n  actionable checklist items, consumed much later by `/complete-implementation`. Same shape as\\n  every other concern already flowing into that section. Architect \\u00a71.1 explicitly rejects\\n  `artifact_register` here: no `artifact_type` enum member fits, and `code-review` is already\\n  owned by `dh:code-reviewer`.\\n- **groom/error.md diagnostic \\u2192 `artifact_register`.** Single-shot structured diagnostic data\\n  feeding one immediate decision \\u2014 the T0/TN shape, not the checklist shape.\\n\\nForcing one mechanism onto both sites would be the over-generalization Impact Radius R5 warns\\nagainst.\\n\\n## Hard exclusions (all four are traps this item has already walked into)\\n\\n1. **Never `TeamCreate`.** Explicitly ruled out by the user. Both sites stay bare `Agent()` spawns.\\n2. **Never `SendMessage(to=\\\"team-lead\\\", ...)`.** There is no team-lead when there is no team. This\\n   is #3249's fix for `impact-analyst` and it is NOT transferable \\u2014 `impact-analyst` is a\\n   `TeamCreate` teammate. It is the most discoverable wrong answer.\\n3. **Never re-introduce SendMessage as transport at all.** Commit `11082f0eb` removed it\\n   deliberately: SendMessage is Claude-Code-only, and this plugin's content also targets Codex,\\n   OpenCode, Crush and Kilo.\\n4. **Never touch #3250's scope.** #3250 audits TeamCreate teammates missing a\\n   SendMessage-to-team-lead step. The two items must remain independently verifiable (AC5).\\n\\n## Files, and only these files\\n\\n| File | Task | Change |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md` | T1 | New `issue_number` input; Output Format rewritten to `backlog_groom`; drop unused `SendMessage` grant |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` | T1 | Add `Issue number: {issue}` to step 4a's dispatch prompt; delete the synchronous branch at lines 187-198 |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/error.md` | T2 | Diagnostic agent registers a YAML `audit-report` artifact; read-back inserted before the decision tree |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/AGENTS.md` | T2 | One table row \\u2014 `audit-report` ownership now names two producers |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch-contract/SKILL.md` | T3 | Split the conflated sentence at line 11; keep specialist-selection, delete the reporting claim |\\n| `plugins/development-harness/skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md` | T4 | **VERIFY UNCHANGED.** Architect \\u00a75 confirms no edit needed |\\n\\n## Explicitly deferred (architect \\u00a77 \\u2014 do not fold in)\\n\\n- A general documentation-and-review gate requiring all `dh:*` agents to declare a completion-report\\n  step, plus a follow-up audit of the remaining ~4 agents named in the frequency analysis. Not in\\n  this item's five Acceptance Criteria; belongs in a separate follow-up item.\\n- `skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` \\u2014 independently verified clean (zero bare `Agent(` calls,\\n  already artifact-register-based). Correct pattern. Do not touch.\\n\\n## Decomposition decisions\\n\\n**Why T1 merges the producer and the consumer.** Splitting them produces an incorrect intermediate\\nstate in either order: land the agent edit alone and BOTH the agent and step 4a write each concern\\n(duplicate entries); land the step 4a edit alone and nothing writes at all (the original defect,\\nnow with the fallback removed). Architect \\u00a72.2 notes they can land in one commit. They are two\\nhalves of one destination move against a single defect site, so they are one task.\\n\\n**Why T3 does not depend on T1 or T2.** The doctrine change cross-references\\n`subagent-contract/SKILL.md`'s `<result_destination>` clause, which already exists unchanged in the\\nworking tree. It does not quote or depend on any prose T1 or T2 writes. T1, T2 and T3 are fully\\nparallel; only T4 depends on all three.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"\",\"issue\":\"3276\",\"tasks\":[{\"id\":\"T1\",\"title\":\"Route contract-verification findings to the Concerns section, and stop implement-feature step 4a from reading a return value\",\"status\":\"not-started\",\"agent\":\"dh:task-worker\",\"dependencies\":[],\"blocked_by\":[],\"parallelize_with\":[],\"priority\":1,\"complexity\":\"medium\",\"skills\":[\"plugin-creator:claude-plugins-reference-2026\"],\"created\":\"2026-08-28T18:46:32.991956+00:00\",\"started\":null,\"completed\":null,\"last_activity\":null,\"body\":\"\",\"description\":\"Two files, one atomic change. `agents/contract-verification.md` currently ends its Output Format section with a synchronous-return override (line 151: \\\"Your finding is your response. The dispatcher reads it there \\u2014 you register no artifact and write no task state.\\\"). `skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` lines 187-198 branch on that never-arriving value. The producer gains the write; the consumer loses the read.\\n\\nThese are merged into one task deliberately: landing either half alone yields an incorrect intermediate state \\u2014 the agent edit alone causes BOTH the agent and step 4a to write each concern (duplicates), the step 4a edit alone leaves nothing writing at all. Architect \\u00a72.2 confirms they can land in one commit.\\n\\nProse only. No Python, no schema changes, no new tools.\",\"objective\":\"Move responsibility for recording contract findings from the orchestrator (which reads a value that never arrives) to the contract-verification agent itself (which writes directly to the backlog item's Concerns section before it returns), and remove the now-dead consumer branch.\",\"requirements\":\"### File A \\u2014 `plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md`\\n\\n**A1. Frontmatter (line 5).** Change `tools:` to exactly:\\n\\n```\\ntools: Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, Skill, mcp__plugin_dh_sam, mcp__plugin_dh_backlog\\n```\\n\\nThat is the current list minus `SendMessage`. Nothing else in the frontmatter changes. Rationale (architect \\u00a71.4): no instruction uses the grant after this change, and an unused SendMessage grant is exactly what invites the next author to reach for the wrong precedent.\\n\\n**A2. Inputs section (currently lines 23-32).** The section opens \\\"You receive three inputs in your delegation prompt\\\" and lists `architect_spec_path`, `task_id`, `modified_files`. Make it four, adding:\\n\\n- `issue_number` \\u2014 the parent backlog item's identifier (`str | int` \\u2014 GitHub integer ID or beads nanoid string), used to address `backlog_groom`.\\n\\nUpdate the \\\"three inputs\\\" count in the prose. Extend the existing BLOCKED sentence so a missing `issue_number` is explicitly a BLOCKED condition, mirroring how `agents/t0-baseline-capture.md` treats its own required `item_id`.\\n\\n**A3. Output Format section (lines 121-151) \\u2014 replace the delivery mechanism only.** Steps 1-5 (lines 34-119, extraction and comparison) are NOT part of this defect and must be left byte-identical. Within Output Format:\\n\\n- The `<concerns>` block structure at lines 127-139 and the \\\"Each concern entry must include\\\" list at 141-145 describe how a finding is *shaped*. Keep that shaping guidance; it now describes the content the agent assembles before writing rather than text it returns.\\n- **Delete line 151 entirely** (`Your finding is your response...`).\\n- Add a delivery procedure that issues **exactly one `backlog_groom` call per finding, and exactly one call when there are no findings \\u2014 never zero calls**:\\n  - Per violation:\\n    ```\\n    mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_groom(\\n        selector=\\\"#{issue_number}\\\",\\n        section=\\\"Concerns\\\",\\n        content=\\\"- [ ] CONTRACT: {severity} \\u2014 {issue line, one sentence} (reported by contract-verification on {task_id})\\\",\\n        append=True\\n    )\\n    ```\\n    This is the exact content shape `implement-feature/SKILL.md` builds today at lines 190-196 \\u2014 moved into the producer, not redesigned.\\n  - When clean, one call with a pre-resolved entry:\\n    ```\\n    content=\\\"- [x] CONTRACT: no concerns \\u2014 all contracts in scope satisfied (reported by contract-verification on {task_id})\\\"\\n    ```\\n    The leading `[x]` versus `[ ]` is the interface contract distinguishing a clean run from a dropped one at a glance. This is what makes Acceptance Criterion 2 true.\\n- **Terminal response.** End with `STATUS: DONE` on its own first line (per `dh:subagent-contract`'s `<status>` clause, a skill this agent already loads), summarizing what was written \\u2014 e.g. `Wrote N contract finding(s) to #{issue_number} Concerns section (task {task_id}).` The response text is no longer load-bearing: the write lands before the agent returns.\\n\\n**A4. Operating Rules (lines 153-162).** The rule \\\"If the architect spec has no Component Design or Type System Design section, output `No contract concerns \\u2014 no contracts defined in spec`\\\" now describes a return value on a channel nobody reads. Route that case through the same clean-result `backlog_groom` call as A3, so it too is affirmatively recorded rather than silent.\\n\\n### File B \\u2014 `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md`\\n\\n**B1. Dispatch prompt (lines 166-185).** Add one line to the delegation prompt body, alongside the existing `Task ID:` / `Plan:` / `Architect spec:` lines:\\n\\n```\\nIssue number: {issue}\\n```\\n\\n`{issue}` is the same local name section 4 already uses at line 141 (`selector=\\\"#{issue}\\\"`), and step 4a already runs inside the `if a parent issue number is known` branch at line 151 \\u2014 the value is in scope at dispatch time. No new plumbing.\\n\\n**B2. Delete lines 187-198 in full** \\u2014 the paragraph beginning \\\"If the contract-verification agent returns a `<concerns>` block\\\", the `backlog_groom` code fence that follows it, and its trailing \\\"Use the MCP tool for this call.\\\" line. That responsibility now lives in the agent (A3).\\n\\n**B3. Preserve line 200 unchanged**: \\\"If `artifact_read` fails or returns no content (no architect spec for this issue), skip step 4a entirely.\\\" That is a pre-dispatch skip condition, unrelated to result routing.\\n\\n**B4. Nothing else in step 4a changes.** No wait loop, no poll, no read-back. Architect \\u00a72.3: nothing in step 4a consumes the concerns immediately \\u2014 line 149 already states they feed `/complete-implementation`, a materially later step, and the existing TN bookend plus Completion Gate (lines 346-349) already provide the ordering guarantee. Proceed to step 4b once the dispatch call returns.\",\"constraints\":\"- **No `TeamCreate`.** contract-verification stays a bare background `Agent()` spawn. Explicitly excluded by the user.\\n- **No `SendMessage`, in any form** \\u2014 not `to=\\\"team-lead\\\"`, not to anyone. There is no team-lead in this dispatch context, and commit `11082f0eb` removed SendMessage deliberately because it is Claude-Code-only while this plugin also targets Codex, OpenCode, Crush and Kilo. Re-adding it would undo that portability work.\\n- **No `artifact_register` for this site.** Architect \\u00a71.1 rejects it with three reasons: no `artifact_type` enum member names per-task contract findings; `code-review` is already owned by `dh:code-reviewer`'s S6 schema and reusing it would corrupt type-alone reads; and Acceptance Criteria 1-2 name Concerns as the destination directly.\\n- **Do not touch Steps 1-5** of contract-verification.md (lines 34-119). Extraction and comparison logic is out of scope.\\n- **Do not touch `skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md`** \\u2014 architect \\u00a75 confirms it needs no change; its primary rule (\\\"Put your result where your own agent file says\\\") is what makes this fix legal.\\n- **Do not touch `skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md`** \\u2014 verified clean, already correct.\\n- **Do not extend the artifact_type enum** \\u2014 that is a Python/backend change, out of scope for this markdown-only item.\\n- Both files are agent-facing instruction prose. Follow the plugin's existing voice and formatting; do not restructure sections beyond what is specified.\",\"expected_outputs\":\"Two modified files:\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md` \\u2014 frontmatter tools list, Inputs section, Output Format section, and one Operating Rules bullet.\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \\u2014 one added line in step 4a's dispatch prompt, one deleted block (lines 187-198).\\n\\nNo new files. No Python. No schema changes.\",\"acceptance_criteria\":\"1. `plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md` frontmatter `tools:` line reads exactly `tools: Read, Grep, Glob, Bash, Skill, mcp__plugin_dh_sam, mcp__plugin_dh_backlog` \\u2014 `SendMessage` appears nowhere in the file.\\n2. The Inputs section lists four inputs including `issue_number` with its `str | int` type note, and a missing `issue_number` is stated as a BLOCKED condition.\\n3. The string `finding is your response` does not appear anywhere in the file.\\n4. The Output Format section instructs a `mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_groom` call with `section=\\\"Concerns\\\"` and `append=True` for the violations case, using the `- [ ] CONTRACT: ... (reported by contract-verification on {task_id})` content shape.\\n5. The Output Format section instructs a `backlog_groom` call for the no-violations case using a `- [x] CONTRACT: no concerns` content shape \\u2014 so the clean path issues exactly one call, never zero.\\n6. The agent's terminal response is specified to begin with `STATUS: DONE` as its own first line.\\n7. `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` step 4a's delegation prompt includes an issue-number line passing `{issue}` to the agent.\\n8. The paragraph beginning `If the contract-verification agent returns a` and its following `backlog_groom` code fence are deleted from `implement-feature/SKILL.md`.\\n9. Step 4a's pre-dispatch skip condition (\\\"If `artifact_read` fails or returns no content... skip step 4a entirely\\\") is still present and unmodified.\\n10. Lines 34-119 of contract-verification.md (Contract Extraction Process through Step 5 Scope Narrowing) are byte-identical to their pre-change content.\\n11. Neither file gained any line containing `TeamCreate`, `team-lead`, or `SendMessage`.\",\"verification_steps\":\"1. `grep -n 'SendMessage\\\\|TeamCreate\\\\|team-lead' plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \\u2014 expect no output from contract-verification.md; any hit in implement-feature/SKILL.md must be pre-existing (confirm via `git diff` that it is not an added line).\\n2. `grep -c 'finding is your response' plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md` \\u2014 expect `0`.\\n3. `grep -n 'issue_number' plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md` \\u2014 expect hits in both the Inputs section and the Output Format `backlog_groom` call.\\n4. `grep -n 'backlog_groom' plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md` \\u2014 expect the violations-case call and the clean-case call to be distinguishable, one carrying `- [ ] CONTRACT:` and one carrying `- [x] CONTRACT:`.\\n5. `grep -n 'If the contract-verification agent returns' plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \\u2014 expect no output.\\n6. `grep -n 'Issue number' plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \\u2014 confirm step 4a's dispatch prompt now passes the issue number.\\n7. `git diff plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md` \\u2014 read the full hunk list and confirm no hunk touches lines within the Contract Extraction Process or Verification Process sections (Steps 1-5).\\n8. `git diff plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \\u2014 confirm the diff contains exactly one addition (the issue-number line) and one deletion block (lines 187-198), and nothing else.\\n\\n**CoVe check \\u2014 answer each in writing before marking this task complete:**\\n\\n- **Q1.** Does the clean path issue exactly one `backlog_groom` call, never zero? Quote the instruction that makes zero calls impossible. If the file can be read as \\\"say nothing when clean,\\\" Acceptance Criterion 2 is not met and the defect survives in a new costume.\\n- **Q2.** Trace `{issue}` from `implement-feature/SKILL.md` step 4a's dispatch prompt into `contract-verification.md`'s `backlog_groom(selector=\\\"#{issue_number}\\\")`. Name the line in each file. If either end is missing, the agent will BLOCK on every run.\\n- **Q3.** After deleting lines 187-198, is there any remaining instruction anywhere in `implement-feature/SKILL.md` that reads the contract-verification agent's textual output? Grep and confirm. A surviving reader means a duplicate write or a dead branch.\\n- **Q4.** Confirm exactly one writer exists per concern \\u2014 the agent \\u2014 and step 4a writes none. Two writers means duplicate Concerns entries on every run.\\n- **Q5.** Re-read the Constraints list. Confirm each of the four hard exclusions (TeamCreate, SendMessage, artifact_register, subagent-contract edits) is respected, citing the evidence for each.\",\"context_notes\":\"Root doctrine: `plugins/development-harness/skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md`'s `<result_destination>` clause \\u2014 \\\"Put your result where your own agent file says\\\" \\u2014 is the primary rule this fix satisfies by naming Concerns explicitly in the agent file. The artifact fallback (\\\"every other document is an artifact\\\") activates only where no agent file names a destination, which is why it does not apply here.\\n\\nWorking precedent for a bare-`Agent()` agent routing results through the backend in this same plugin: `agents/t0-baseline-capture.md` and `agents/tn-verification-gate.md` (both use `artifact_register`; the mechanism differs, the discipline is identical).\\n\\nHistory worth knowing: commit `11082f0eb` removed contract-verification's SendMessage step for sound cross-harness portability reasons but substituted \\\"your finding is your response\\\" \\u2014 a channel that does not exist under async dispatch. Commit `43058f345` fixed the sibling symptom for `impact-analyst` with `SendMessage(to=\\\"team-lead\\\")`, which works there only because impact-analyst is a `TeamCreate` teammate. Copying it here would reproduce the defect.\",\"analysis_method\":\"none\",\"divergence_notes\":0,\"accuracy_risk\":\"high\",\"issue_classification\":\"defect\"}],\"source_path\":null,\"state\":\"drafting\",\"acceptance_criteria_structured\":[{\"criterion_id\":\"AC1-cv-writes-to-backend\",\"description\":\"contract-verification.md instructs the agent to write its finding via backlog_groom (AC1: violations reach a durable location with no human transcription)\",\"check_command\":\"grep -q 'backlog_groom' plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md\",\"expected_baseline\":\"any\",\"expected_final\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"AC2-clean-result-recorded\",\"description\":\"contract-verification.md specifies an affirmative pre-resolved entry for the no-violations case, so silence never encodes 'clean' (AC2)\",\"check_command\":\"grep -q '\\\\[x\\\\] CONTRACT' plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md\",\"expected_baseline\":\"any\",\"expected_final\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"AC3-sync-claim-removed\",\"description\":\"The line-151 synchronous-return override is gone (AC3)\",\"check_command\":\"! grep -q 'finding is your response' plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md\",\"expected_baseline\":\"any\",\"expected_final\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"AC3-consumer-branch-removed\",\"description\":\"implement-feature step 4a no longer branches on a return value that never arrives\",\"check_command\":\"! grep -q 'If the contract-verification agent returns' plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md\",\"expected_baseline\":\"any\",\"expected_final\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"AC3-issue-number-threaded\",\"description\":\"contract-verification.md declares issue_number as a required input so it can address backlog_groom\",\"check_command\":\"grep -q 'issue_number' plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md\",\"expected_baseline\":\"any\",\"expected_final\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"AC4-diagnostic-registers\",\"description\":\"groom/error.md's diagnostic agent registers findings as an artifact instead of returning them (AC4)\",\"check_command\":\"grep -q 'artifact_register' plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/error.md\",\"expected_baseline\":\"any\",\"expected_final\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"AC4-decision-tree-reads-back\",\"description\":\"groom/error.md reads the diagnostic back before its Mermaid decision tree branches, making the Escalation branch reachable (AC4)\",\"check_command\":\"grep -q 'artifact_read' plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/groom/error.md\",\"expected_baseline\":\"any\",\"expected_final\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"doctrine-claim-removed\",\"description\":\"dispatch-contract/SKILL.md no longer authorizes 'finding is its response' as a valid result destination (Risk R2)\",\"check_command\":\"! grep -q 'whose finding is its response' plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch-contract/SKILL.md\",\"expected_baseline\":\"any\",\"expected_final\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"doctrine-selection-preserved\",\"description\":\"The true specialist-selection guidance survives the doctrine edit (architect \\u00a74.1)\",\"check_command\":\"grep -q 'dh roster or not' plugins/development-harness/skills/dispatch-contract/SKILL.md\",\"expected_baseline\":\"any\",\"expected_final\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"AC5-no-sendmessage-grant\",\"description\":\"The unused SendMessage tool grant is revoked from contract-verification.md's frontmatter (architect \\u00a71.4)\",\"check_command\":\"! grep -q 'SendMessage' plugins/development-harness/agents/contract-verification.md\",\"expected_baseline\":\"any\",\"expected_final\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"AC5-scope-boundary\",\"description\":\"AC5 / architect \\u00a76: no added line introduces TeamCreate, team-lead, or SendMessage \\u2014 #3250's scope is untouched\",\"check_command\":\"! git diff main -- plugins/development-harness | grep -qE '^\\\\+.*(TeamCreate|team-lead|SendMessage)'\",\"expected_baseline\":\"any\",\"expected_final\":\"pass\"},{\"criterion_id\":\"subagent-contract-unchanged\",\"description\":\"architect \\u00a75: subagent-contract/SKILL.md is confirmed correct as-is and must carry zero changes\",\"check_command\":\"git diff --quiet main -- plugins/development-harness/skills/subagent-contract/SKILL.md\",\"expected_baseline\":\"any\",\"expected_final\":\"pass\"}]}"}